# --- Third-party benchmark data: never redistributed ---------------------
# benchmark-manifest.yaml declares ships_public_records: false. SOURCE_LOCK.json
# records the provider, URL, and SHA-256 of every artifact so a reviewer acquires
# the identical bytes themselves. The bytes never enter this repository.
yauvi-structural-workbench/benchmarks/*/sources/
yauvi-structural-workbench/benchmarks/*/build/

# The same rule, for where an engine writes its own intermediates. The sf-csa
# campaign leaves 109 MB under `results/sf_csa/release-1/work/`: the downloaded
# UniProt proteomes it searched and the DIAMOND indices built from them. Same
# class of bytes as `sources/`, arriving by a path the two rules above do not
# cover. Nothing checksums them -- `CHECKSUMS.json` covers the 112 evidence
# files and no entry names `work/` -- and they rebuild from the source lock.
yauvi-structural-workbench/benchmarks/*/results/**/work/

# --- Build outputs -------------------------------------------------------
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
*.whl
*.tar.gz

